ne())
+            .or_default() += 1;
+    }
+    output
+}
+
+fn provider_statuses(run: &MonitorRun) -> Vec<ProviderStatus> {
+    let mut status = BTreeMap::new();
+    for receipt in &run.receipts {
+        status.insert(
+            receipt.provider_id.clone(),
+            ProviderStatus {
+                provider_id: receipt.provider_id.clone(),
+                succeeded: true,
+                records_retrieved: receipt.records_retrieved,
+                failure: None,
+            },
+        );
+    }
+    for failure in &run.provider_failures {
+        status.insert(
+            failure.provider_id.clone(),
+            ProviderStatus {
+                provider_id: failure.provider_id.clone(),
+                succeeded: false,
+                records_retrieved: 0,
+                failure: Some(failure.clone()),
+            },
+        );
+    }
+    status.into_values().collect()
+}
+
+fn append_markdown_papers(output: &mut String, heading: &str, papers: &[ReportPaper]) {
+    output.push_str(&format!("## {heading}\n\n"));
+    if papers.is_empty() {
+        output.push_str("No records.\n\n");
+        return;
+    }
+    for paper in papers {
+        output.push_str(&format!(
+            "- **{}** ({}) — {:?}, score {}; {}; {}.\n",
+            paper.title,
+            paper.publication_year.map_or_else(|| "n.d.".to_owned(), |year| year.to_string()),
+            paper.attribution,
+            paper.attribution_score,
+            paper.primary_theme.as_deref().unwrap_or("Unclassified theme"),
+            paper.study_type,
+        ));
+    }
+    output.push('\n');
+}
+
+fn count_rows(counts: &BTreeMap<String, usize>) -> String {
+    counts
+        .iter()
+        .map(|(label, count)| {
+            format!(
+                "<tr><td>{}</td><td>{count}</td></tr>",
+                escape_html(label)
+            )
+        })
+        .collect()
+}
+
+fn html_paper_rows(papers: &[ReportPaper]) -> String {
+    if papers.is_empty() {
+        return "<tr><td colspan=\"5\">No records.</td></tr>".to_owned();
+    }
+    papers
+        .iter()
+        .map(|paper| {
+            let title = paper.url.as_ref().map_or_else(
+                || escape_html(&paper.title),
+                |url| {
+                    format!(
+                        "<a href=\"{}\" rel=\"noreferrer\">{}</a>",
+                        escape_html(url),
+                        escape_html(&paper.title)
+                    )
+                },
+            );
+            format!(
+                "<tr><td>{title}<br><small>{}</small></td><td><span class=\"pill\">{:?} {}</span></td><td>{}</td><td>{}</td><td>{}</td></tr>",
+                escape_html(&paper.authors.join("; ")),
+                paper.attribution,
+                paper.attribution_score,
+                escape_html(paper.primary_theme.as_deref().unwrap_or("Unclassified")),
+                escape_html(&paper.study_type),
+                escape_html(&paper.sources.join(", ")),
+            )
+        })
+        .collect()
+}
+
+fn csv_escape(value: &str) -> String {
+    if value.chars().any(|character| matches!(character, ',' | '"' | '\n' | '\r')) {
+        format!("\"{}\"", value.replace('"', "\"\""))
+    } else {
+        value.to_owned()
+    }
+}
+
+fn escape_html(value: &str) -> String {
+    value
+        .replace('&', "&amp;")
+        .replace('<', "&lt;")
+        .replace('>', "&gt;")
+        .replace('"', "&quot;")
+        .replace('\'', "&#39;")
+}
+
+/// Report construction or output error.
+#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]
+pub enum ReportError {
+    /// State contract failed validation.
+    #[error(transparent)]
+    Model(#[from] crate::model::ModelError),
+    /// Month was not in `YYYY-MM` form.
+    #[error("`{0}` is not a valid YYYY-MM month")]
+    InvalidMonth(String),
+    /// State contained no completed run.
+    #[error("monitor state contains no reportable run")]
+    NoRuns,
+    /// File operation failed.
+    #[error(transparent)]
+    Io(#[from] std::io::Error),
+    /// JSON encoding failed.
+    #[error(transparent)]
+    Json(#[from] serde_json::Error),
+}
